[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Main Modules

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
HVPS Bootloader Firmware - The firmware occupies the first 48 KiB of MCU flash. It validates a
signed MCUboot image in a single 180 KiB primary slot and either transfers execution to the
application or remains available for serial recovery.

Firmware Packaging Tools - The image creation utility converts an application Intel HEX artifact
into an MCUboot image with a 512-byte header and signs it using ECDSA P-256. The upload utility or
the standard mcumgr client transfers the packaged image to image 0 over UART3.

Flash Memory - The MCU flash contains a bootloader region beginning at 0x08000000 and a primary
application slot beginning at 0x0800C000. The application vector table normally begins at
0x0800C200 after the MCUboot header.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-11
TITLE: Application Validation and Boot Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
After peripheral initialization, the bootloader opens a three-second MCUboot serial-recovery window
and then invokes boot_go(). MCUboot validates the primary-slot image header, SHA-256 TLV, and EC256
signature against the public key compiled into the bootloader. On success the firmware reports
BOOT_GO_OK and performs the protected application handoff. On failure it reports BOOT_GO_FAIL once
and repeats the serial-recovery and validation loop without executing the image.
<<<
