[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-13
TITLE: Primary-Slot Flash Processing
STATEMENT: >>>
The flash-map backend exposes one 180 KiB primary slot beginning at 0x0800C000. MCUboot receives
image-management upload chunks for image 0 and supplies slot-relative offsets to this backend.

Writes are constrained to the primary-slot bounds and require a 4-byte-aligned destination, source,
and length. The backend unlocks flash, programs 32-bit words, and locks flash after each operation.
Erasures are constrained to slot bounds and 2048-byte physical-page boundaries. Progressive erase
is enabled so MCUboot erases the pages required by the upload rather than using the retired explicit
91-page erase command.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-2
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
