[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-9
TITLE: UART3 Transport
STATEMENT: >>>
The serial bootloader uses UART3 at 38400 baud, 8 data bits, no parity, and one stop bit. Reception
is interrupt-driven one byte at a time into a 1024-byte ring buffer. The MCUboot line reader removes
bytes from the ring buffer and returns one newline-terminated NLIP line at a time. A full ring buffer
drops newly received bytes until space becomes available.

Transmission uses blocking HAL UART transmission. The upload-activity LED pattern is updated while
a line is being received and returns to the idle pattern after a complete line or receive timeout.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-4
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-9
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-10
TITLE: MCUboot Serial-Management Processing
STATEMENT: >>>
MCUboot serial management uses standard NLIP line framing. Each management packet contains an SMP
header and CBOR payload, is protected by CRC16-XMODEM, base64 encoded, and divided into newline-
terminated NLIP lines. The configured maximum received management message is 512 bytes.

The enabled management operations provide echo, image status/listing, image-0 upload, and system
reset. Upload requests carry an image offset and data chunk. MCUboot validates request sequencing,
decoding, framing CRC, image bounds, and final image metadata before the image is eligible to boot.
Malformed packets receive a management error response or are discarded without transferring
execution to their contents.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-2
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
