[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-14
TITLE: MCUboot Bootutil Integration
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware integrates the MCUboot bootutil library to provide industry-standard secure boot
capabilities. The bootutil module provides functions to validate application images stored in flash
memory, including verification of image headers, cryptographic signature validation, and integrity
checks. Image integrity is represented in the MCUboot TLV area rather than the legacy stored
application CRC. The bootutil library uses a single application slot architecture with primary slot
validation enabled. The firmware configures MCUboot with the following parameters:

- MCUBOOT_IMAGE_NUMBER = 1: Single application image
- MCUBOOT_SINGLE_APPLICATION_SLOT = 1: Single slot architecture
- MCUBOOT_SIGN_EC256 = 1: EC256 signature algorithm
- MCUBOOT_VALIDATE_PRIMARY_SLOT = 1: Validate primary slot on every boot
- MCUBOOT_SERIAL = 1: Serial bootloader interface enabled
- MCUBOOT_OVERWRITE_ONLY = 1: Overwrite-only image update mode
- MCUBOOT_ERASE_PROGRESSIVELY = 1: Erase pages as required during upload
- MCUBOOT_SERIAL_MAX_RECEIVE_SIZE = 512: Maximum decoded management message size
- MCUBOOT_FIH_PROFILE_OFF = 1: Fault-injection-hardening profile disabled

The bootutil library processes the application image header and TLV area to verify the image
integrity and authenticity before allowing the bootloader to jump to the application code.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-5
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-15
TITLE: Vector Table Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
Before jumping to the application, the firmware reads the stack pointer and reset handler addresses
from the application image vector table. The firmware then validates:

1. Stack Pointer: Validates that the stack pointer is within the inclusive RAM range 0x20000000
   through 0x20008000.
2. Reset Handler: Ensures the reset handler address is within the valid application code range,
   which must be greater than or equal to the image start address and less than the end of the
   current executable-image bound (0x08024000).

If either validation fails, the firmware outputs ERR_SP or ERR_RH and returns control to the
bootloader instead of jumping to the application.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-6
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-7
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-17
TITLE: Serial Bootloader Interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware implements a serial bootloader interface using the UART3 peripheral to allow
firmware updates via the MCUboot management protocol. After initialization and before each image
validation attempt, boot_serial_check_start() provides a three-second recovery interval.

The serial bootloader supports the following operations:
- Management echo for bootloader-presence detection
- Image status/listing
- Image-0 upload, including progressive erase and programming of application flash
- System reset

If validation fails, the main loop repeats the recovery interval indefinitely. If validation
succeeds and no recovery operation prevents boot, the firmware transfers execution to the image.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-4
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-9
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-12
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-18
TITLE: Application Handoff
STATEMENT: >>>
After all image and vector-table checks succeed, the bootloader disables interrupts, stops and
clears SysTick, disables and clears NVIC interrupt state, and writes the application vector-table
address to VTOR. It issues data and instruction synchronization barriers, re-enables interrupts,
loads MSP from the first vector-table word, and branches directly to the reset handler from the
second vector-table word without retaining a C call frame on the new stack.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-10
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-19
TITLE: Firmware Image Packaging and Trust
STATEMENT: >>>
The application is linked to begin at 0x0800C200. The image-generation tooling places a 512-byte
MCUboot header at the primary-slot base, adds SHA-256 metadata in the TLV area, and signs release
images using ECDSA with the NIST P-256 curve. The bootloader contains only the matching public key.

Production private keys shall be maintained outside source control in an access-controlled signing
environment. Any private key stored with development tooling shall be identified as a non-production
test key and shall not be used to authorize production firmware.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-1
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPSIB-5
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPSIB-20
TITLE: Interrupted Upload Behavior
STATEMENT: >>>
The single-slot upload writes directly into the primary slot and progressively erases affected flash
pages. Until the upload contains a complete image with valid MCUboot metadata and signature,
boot_go() rejects the slot. The bootloader then remains in its recovery loop so the PC can restart or
resume a valid upload. The design does not provide rollback to the previously installed image because
there is no secondary slot.
<<<
